      "base_year": 2024,
      "producer": "Microcosm UK release microcosm-uk-2024-25-national, cut microcosm-uk-2024-25-national-20261019T083323Z-6cba5d71 (build uk-frs-calibration-attempt-20261019T083323Z-6cba5d71 on microcosm 810315ac, the head of PolicyEngine/microcosm#1316, merged later that day, with policyengine-uk 2.132.6), published 2026-10-19 on the main branch of the Hugging Face dataset repo policyengine/populace-uk-private (commit 52f48aa1); a certified release: its 39 spine, 7 calibration-seam and 19 release-cut gates passed",
      "observation": "FRS 2024-25 spine; capital gains amounts drawn from HMRC Table 3 (size of gain by taxable income, 2024-25) with asset types from HMRC Tables 7 and 8, gains qualifying for Business Asset Disposal Relief and Investors' Relief imputed from HMRC Table 4, and the sub-exempt remainder drawn from the Advani-Summers within-band distribution; household weights calibrated to 1,215 targets, among them HMRC's CGT totals, size bands, gains by taxable income band (Table 3), age, region, the BADR bands (Table 4) and residential property gains",
      "notes": "The build's projection fence bounds the gainers that uprating carries over the frozen exempt amount by 2030 at 7.0k, against HMRC's 73k taxpayers with gains of \u00a33,000 to \u00a35,999 in 2024-25 (Table 2.1a); this repo's uprating audit counts 7.1k on policyengine-uk 2.132.6.",
      "columns": "It carries capital_gains, capital_gains_residential_property (the residential schedule) and capital_gains_badr (gains qualifying for Business Asset Disposal Relief or Investors' Relief), and no carried-interest column.",
